From: PickleHik3 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Torch manager: do not post the state it already has

A tap on the torch quick setting posted /v1/torch twice. The reply moves the manager's
brightness, settings.c's on_torch_brightness_changed() sets the (hidden) torch scale to match, and
the scale's value-changed handler on_torch_scale_value_changed() calls
phosh_torch_manager_set_scaled_brightness() with the state just reached, which posted it again.
set_scaled_brightness now returns when the wanted state is the current one.

diff --git a/src/torch-manager-tl.c b/src/torch-manager-tl.c
index 01feb77..224c3d2 100644
--- a/src/torch-manager-tl.c
+++ b/src/torch-manager-tl.c
@@ -323,6 +323,12 @@ phosh_torch_manager_set_scaled_brightness (PhoshTorchManager *self, double frac)
   if (!self->present)
     return;
 
+  /* The settings panel's (hidden) brightness scale calls this whenever the state it follows
+   * changes, which posted the state the launcher had just answered a second time. The torch is
+   * on or off here, so a wanted state equal to the current one is nothing to post. */
+  if ((frac > 0.0) == !!self->brightness)
+    return;
+
   set_enabled (self, frac > 0.0);
 }
 
